WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.820
So Ra No Wo To

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:16.640
...is how we'll do it.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.650
Roger that.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:19.660
We'll begin the mission-

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.410
Heading out, Kana-chan?

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.590
Good morning!

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:29.400
She's off to use her first paycheck.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.790
Not all of it.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:35.960
I'm sending some home, and I wanted
to send a present along with it, and...

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.720
A little present for yourself, too?

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:39.880
Yup!

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:44.380
You were a trainee for the first month,
so you didn't get paid a thing.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.580
Must be nice, huh?

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.520
But I'm surprised.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:53.980
I'd heard that we're usually paid late,
and that it's normally in scrip...

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.640
Here you go!

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.860
Thank you!

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.740
I didn't think I'd get real money.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.270
Of course, you do.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:10.870
That's why we have our other jobs-

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:15.180
Kanata, um, well...

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.080
There's a market in town today!

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.670
It's your first time at one, right?

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:23.990
It's the perfect time to use your
first day off and paycheck.

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:27.060
Forget about work and go enjoy yourself.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.060
OK!

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:34.060
Kanata's Day Off - Hair Braiding

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.390
OK, see you later!

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.880
I told you not to tip her off!

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.790
But no one would believe

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:57.720
we get paid on time out here,
in the middle of nowhere!

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:06.600
She believed it, though...

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.660
That's part of what makes her Kana-chan.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.770
Yeah.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:15.890
Not like you two, who immediately wondered
where the money came from.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.400
Right?

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:23.030
Now, then...

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.530
Let's forget about our main jobs, too.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.560
Good stuff.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.650
Ain't it?

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:40.130
But there's one problem.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.860
I'm not lowering the price.

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:51.060
Um, excuse me. I was enjoying myself, and...

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.350
Looks like you're ready.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:07.280
Yeah, no problems at all.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.570
<i>We</i> have a problem.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.080
And I've got a suggestion to go with it.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.520
Want to take it?

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.830
Give us the details, would you?

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:25.410
This one's cute, too.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:47.080
You guys are the sellers, then?

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.040
I take it you like the goods?

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.540
They aren't bad.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.470
But there's a problem.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:06.300
Oh, my. And what's that?

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:11.760
It'll take lots of work and connections
to sell these.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.820
Enough so that it's not quite
worth our time...

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:16.810
So-

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.600
It's not my policy to give discounts.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.810
The price is part of the taste.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:26.320
No one's asking you to cut the price.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.060
We're taking it all!

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:31.240
Don't even think it!

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:39.520
Go ahead, shoot.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:42.520
'Course, before ya do,

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:45.630
my gun'll blow a hole straight through
that pretty head of yours.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:47.630
Then...

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:51.640
Not too swift, are you?

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.000
That's what you get for underestimating us.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:03.400
Good night, children.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:35.600
I warned you.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.980
Hey, you with them?

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:50.830
Mishio-chan!

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.500
Th-The car!

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:01.910
Boss!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:03.920
Give it up!

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.070
But what about the present for the big boss?

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:07.920
Won't do us any good if we're dead!

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.050
Boss!

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.800
No one told me they were this crazy!

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:15.050
I'm never coming back to this town!

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.160
They're gone.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.100
I see.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:26.360
Then we're done, everyone.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:31.030
I was scared there.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:33.860
Looks like we fooled them!

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.790
Thank you for your help.

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:42.870
No, we wouldn't stand a chance
against the central area mafia.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:46.130
You scratch our backs, we'll scratch yours.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:51.880
But you'll be reimbursing us for our parts
in this little play, yes?

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:56.360
Oh, my. Mikhail-san, you're such a kidder.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.300
Not at all.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.600
I'm not kidding at all.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.090
This is business now.

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:05.950
Shall I pay it?

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:10.570
Were you the ones who crushed their car?

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.970
It wasn't you?

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:15.070
What happened?

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:20.330
Someone smashed their car up pretty good.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:26.540
Inside were all these spoils of war
they bought at the market.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.910
I'll take them

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.550
and give you half the profits.
How's that sound?

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.270
Then we have a deal.

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:37.260
Indeed.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.960
I guess that play is over.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:45.280
But I was surprised.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.270
By what?

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.770
That you were really into it.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:55.530
If the military discovered we distilled this,
we'd get a lot more than a court martial.

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:59.100
It's a violation of the monopoly
and tax laws, too.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.530
And at worst, treason.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:02.940
That's right.

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:05.750
We took this job over from
the last group here.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.430
Rio's never opposed it.

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:11.040
I was a bit surprised, too.

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:20.550
Well, at first I was shocked.

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:26.740
When I learned my mother's
beloved calvados was made here...

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:35.560
Then it may be your mother who
led you to being deployed here.

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:56.080
OK, see you later!

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:05.220
Yumina-oneechan!

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:07.780
I'm done.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:08.350
See!

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:11.970
It looks wonderful, Seiya-san.

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:23.300
Mishio-san, it's time for their
first visit to the church.

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:25.340
The priest will be there, too.

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:26.620
So at least for today-

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:28.300
No!

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:32.540
Don't cause problems for her, Mishio!

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.900
Why not do your hair right?

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:35.630
No!

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:36.840
Never!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:37.920
Why?

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.600
You always tell me to!

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:42.110
Shut up, Seiya!

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:48.970
You mustn't do that, Mishio-san.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:53.850
Mishio-san!

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:01.580
10 yen 25 sen...

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:06.240
Hey girl, that's dangerous.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:09.580
Um, excuse me. I was enjoying myself, and...

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.830
They're the problem.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:18.210
They seem to have found
out about the deal.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:23.730
Are you OK?

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:24.340
Yes.

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:29.490
But anyway, Naomi-san! What should I do?

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:34.050
I've never had enough money
in my wallet to buy it.

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:36.900
If I asked for it, I could buy it, couldn't I?

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:42.650
Hey. What if someone came
and tried to buy it for themselves?

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:46.620
Did someone say they wanted it?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.550
No. It was just an example.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.360
Let me see...

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:53.840
I'd...

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:57.730
I'd tell them that dolphins are very
scary animals that eat people,

00:12:57.730 --> 00:12:58.880
so they wouldn't want it!

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:02.010
Ah! You're a genius!

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.090
Oh, I'll keep that dolphin

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:09.680
until you say you don't want it anymore,
so think about it in peace.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:15.980
Then I'll buy a present for
everyone else first.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:21.340
Let's see... Dad, Mom, Granny and Grandpa,

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:24.550
and then my Grandma and
Grandpa in Waren,

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:28.740
Great-Grannie, and then old
lady Nanae next door too!

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:35.450
Wow! Look at all the stuff they're selling!

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:36.420
Like this?

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:39.340
Sorry...

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:43.840
Mishio-chan?

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:46.080
Shopping?

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:48.890
She says she's looking for a box.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:50.150
A box?

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:53.350
Did you see one like this anywhere?

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.480
Sorry.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.030
Want me to help you look?

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.780
What are you doing, Kanata?

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:09.610
I'm buying presents.

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:11.070
I was hoping there would be

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:13.640
something wonderful to send
to my family back home.

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:15.540
But I'm not in a hurry...

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:15.940
No!

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:29.470
What's wrong with her?

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:35.750
I-I don't know about this...

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:38.020
That's a nice shirt, isn't it?

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:40.150
Note: Shirt says "Yoroshiku" (greeting)
written in "gangster/thug" Japanese.

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:40.150
This one's cute, too.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:45.650
Yumina-san?

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:50.860
Um, Kanata-san, did you see Mishio-san?

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:55.200
A box?

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:58.040
Yes. She said it was important.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:00.070
I see.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:07.320
When her mother died, all her
family's property was taken.

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:13.100
A memento of her mother was
one of the items taken.

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:16.970
Every time there's a market,
she thinks she might find it.

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:22.480
I shouldn't have said what I did.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:26.730
I got paid for the first time yesterday.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.840
And so I told her I was getting
presents to send my family.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:31.530
That's fine.

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:37.880
I... We are her family now, I think.

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:46.750
If she's still jealous, that just
means I'm not good enough.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:04.020
Hey, Mom? Which is more important,
me or your box?

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:06.330
You!

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:12.590
Mom...

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:21.350
Mishio-chan...

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:31.960
Mishio-chan!

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:39.010
The famous Treize firecrackers!

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.280
Did you hear them pop?

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:40.930
Who wants some?

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:48.740
Onee-chan...

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:50.270
Yumina-oneechan...

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:51.950
Onee-chan!

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:53.650
Mishio-chan!

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:02.410
The car!

00:17:08.490 --> 00:17:11.040
I'm sorry I'm not Yumina-san.

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:17.150
Onee-chan!

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:19.430
Yumina-oneechan!

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:21.830
Thank you.

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:23.300
You're welcome.

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:28.090
Now then...

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.440
Um...

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:34.700
O-Oh! What's wrong?

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:40.580
Uh, that car... Was it yours?

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:42.950
Was that you guys?

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.320
I'm so sorry!

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:48.330
There's 150 yen in here!

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.090
I'll pay you back...

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:52.980
Great work, guys.

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:55.010
You can keep it.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:57.840
I've already gotten my payment.

00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:04.820
N-Naomi-san, that box!

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:12.890
These ideographs mean
"beautiful rice stalk."

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:19.660
Carve them into her seal, and she'll live a
happy life, like a full field of rice.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.170
My...

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:25.410
Miho, you're lucky to have received
such a nice name.

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:33.900
Did you find Mishio-san?

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:41.030
I've done everything I can
think of to be her family,

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:44.060
but I'm not good enough yet.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:48.040
No, you're doing your best.

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:53.320
Mishio-san!

00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:00.700
Wow, you found it!

00:19:01.230 --> 00:19:03.110
Take good care of it.

00:19:03.110 --> 00:19:05.970
It's an important memory of your mother-

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:07.580
No!

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:12.080
I want you to have this.

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:25.560
Mishio-san was taken in by the church
after she lost her family.

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:31.830
First her father joined the army
and didn't come back...

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:33.300
And her mother?

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:39.110
Her family lived on the Eastern
border of Vingt.

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:40.940
You can't mean...

00:19:40.940 --> 00:19:45.200
Yes, the town that was attacked
by the "Invisible Reaper."

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:48.700
And when the two of them came to Seize,

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:53.280
her mother had already taken
ill, and shortly after...

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:57.460
Mom told me...

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:01.950
that she was sorry she couldn't
braid my hair anymore.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:04.010
And so... And so she told me

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:09.690
to have it braided by the person
who would care for me most.

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:13.480
Braid it for me, Yumina.

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:21.490
Man lives on...

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.600
Even if we part with those we love

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:27.850
and suffer terribly because of it,

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:30.930
we live on.

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:33.070
We can live on.

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:37.750
That bravery is a very sad, very dear thing.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.610
I'm sorry.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:47.050
Thank you, Onee-chan.

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:00.890
Everyone's already in there.

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:02.780
OK! I'll join them soon!

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:08.570
You're tired.

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:13.070
Yeah. I wanted to avoid washing my hair,

00:21:13.070 --> 00:21:14.810
but it didn't work out that way.

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:19.880
Then... Then... Then I'll dry it for you!

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.050
I always wanted to touch it!

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:29.220
So you didn't buy the dolphin?

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:32.060
I thought it was your present to yourself.

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:38.910
Rio-sempai, do you believe in fate?

00:21:38.910 --> 00:21:40.650
What's this, all of a sudden?

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:46.300
You know, something happened today
that made me believe in it.

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:50.220
That was enough of a reward for me.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:53.840
I don't.

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:58.100
I hate things that are decided or
given to you from the beginning.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.340
But yeah...

00:22:04.190 --> 00:22:08.860
It's possible that something,
which someone did by mere coincidence,

00:22:08.860 --> 00:22:13.280
may go round and round, and eventually
change someone's life in a big way.

00:22:17.490 --> 00:22:25.000
If you call that fate, then maybe...

00:22:31.090 --> 00:22:32.370
D-flat.

00:22:39.200 --> 00:22:43.090
I guess you had a wonderful day, too.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:19.930
Chirping Crickets - Spirits Down the River

00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:16.650
Next time:

00:24:16.650 --> 00:24:17.690
Chirping Crickets.

00:24:17.690 --> 00:24:19.370
Spirits Down the River.

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:24.980
This program is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to people, parties,
or situations is purely coincidental.
